Vita (--vita-fast-flow-bind=off|on|verify): dusk::flow::bind_resource with the same binding.
It parses the whole message resource (every message entry, flow node and edge) on each call, and
the knob doors call it every tick through dMsgFlow_c::init (setActionFromFlow -> checkOpenDoor),
a PC-port cost the original game does not have. A successful binding is kept per (resource,
group): while no message resource was set since (dMeter2Info_setMsgResource /
setStageMsgResource, where the game installs and drops the BMGs it binds), the resource's first
16 bytes are the same, no mod patch exists and s_resources still holds exactly the kept entry,
the parse would store the same entry and return true, so the call returns at once. Failed parses
always run (and log) as before. verify runs the original call and compares it with what the kept
binding would have answered. Off (0) unless the Vita entry selects it; the counts go to
platform/vita/runtime/fast_actors.cpp.

--- a/src/dusk/mods/svc/flow.cpp
